From 0a5c159340059686e8b3abeba9722691336b4621 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Fesunenko <body051@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:43:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] lerdge: Support the stock Lerdge bootloader

Add STM32_LERDGE_RAM_RESERVE to keep the end of RAM free for the Lerdge
bootloader, scripts/update_lerdge.py to create the encrypted firmware
files it installs from the TF card, and "lerdge-k"/"lerdge-x" board
definitions for flash-sdcard.sh.  flash-sdcard.sh can now create the
directories the bootloader expects and removes the file after a verified
update, as the bootloader would install it again on every start.  The
card is written with software SPI; the bootloader reads it in SDIO mode,
which requires a power cycle after the upload.  Also fix an error
message in SDCardFile.close().

scripts/lerdge_bootflag.py inspects and clears the bootloader's
"no update" flag in the board's SPI flash.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
